  "name": "Service Level Agreement",
  "description": "A service level agreement or service level schedule — the availability commitment, what is excluded from it, the credit owed when it is missed, and how a credit is claimed. It is an attachment to a subscription or services agreement, so it is not expected to carry an indemnity, a liability cap, payment terms or a governing-law clause of its own. Distinct from `saas-customer` and `msa-customer-deep`, which read the agreement the schedule attaches to.",
